  <!-- Map Icon Legend and status / priority map icon pages -->
  <data name="LegendPageTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Map Icon Legend</value>
  </data>
  <data name="LegendIntro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Every icon the map shows for calls, units and personnel. A call's icon follows its type and priority, a unit's its type and status, and a member's their role and status. Staffing levels never change an icon.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPickedHeader" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How an icon is picked</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPicked1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An icon uploaded for the type or role for that exact priority or status.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPicked2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Otherwise the type's or role's own uploaded icon, with a badge in the color of the priority or status.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPicked3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Otherwise the built-in pin in the color of the priority or status.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowPicked4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A priority or status with no meaning set is colored by what its name suggests, such as Emergency or Out of Service; one whose name suggests nothing shows a gray pin, as does a unit or member that has set no status. Set meanings on the Custom Statuses and Call Priorities pages to be sure.</value>
